  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This knitted cloche is worked bottom-up in the round in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "stocking-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "stocking stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with a turned-up purl brim, fitting adult heads of 54 (56, 58) cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bottom-up construction creates the turned-up brim naturally: the first few rounds are worked inside-out so when the brim turns up the right side faces outward. The deep 26 cm crown follows the 1920s silhouette -- sitting low on the forehead and close to the head. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " method handles the full hat on one needle. About 90 g (200 m) of DK wool. Sits just above the eyebrows."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK-weight wool yarn",
              "qty": "90 g (approx. 200 m)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 8 / US 6)",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "3.5 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 9 / US 4) -- for brim",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Stitch markers",
              "qty": "9 (1 BOR + 8 crown)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle and scissors",
              "qty": "1 each",
              "substitutions": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "22 sts x 30 rounds = 10 x 10 cm in stocking stitch on 4 mm needles, blocked. A cloche must fit closely -- there is no ease in the design. At 23 sts per 10 cm the crown measures 52 cm instead of 54 cm for size S, which will feel tight rather than close-fitting. Match your gauge before casting on."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "k -- knit"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "p -- purl"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "k2tog -- knit two together, right-leaning decrease"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "ssk -- slip, slip, knit, left-leaning decrease"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Before you cast on, circle your size -- every count reads S (M, L)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast on"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " on the 3.5 mm needle, cast on 116 (120, 128) sts using long-tail cast-on. Tail formula: tail_cm = (needle mm x stitch count) / 10 + 15. For size L on a 3.5 mm needle: (3.5 x 128) / 10 + 15 = 60 cm; round up to 65 cm. Join without twisting, place BOR marker."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brim"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work 8 rounds in reverse stocking stitch (purl every round) on the 3.5 mm needle. This section will turn back on itself to form the brim. Switch to 4 mm needle and knit (right side) from this point onward. After the brim, you should have 116 (120, 128) stitches on the needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crown body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work in stocking stitch until hat measures 24 cm from the cast-on edge (including brim section)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crown shaping"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Place 8 markers dividing work into 8 equal sections."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Decrease round 1: *k to 2 sts before marker, k2tog; repeat from * 8 times. 108 (112, 120) sts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 2: knit all."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Continue alternating decrease and plain rounds until 32 sts remain, then decrease every round until 8 sts remain."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "After the final decrease round, you should have 8 stitches on the needle, ready to gather."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Top finish"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cut yarn with 20 cm tail. Draw through all 8 sts, pull firmly, and fasten on the inside."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Common faults"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brim does not turn back neatly: the reverse stocking stitch section must be worked on a needle one size smaller than the crown so the purl edge is firm enough to hold its turn. A loose brim flops forward."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crown sits too high for a cloche silhouette: the crown body must be worked to at least 24 cm. A standard-length beanie reads as a beanie; only the extra depth creates the cloche look."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hat stretches too loose on wet blocking: DK stocking stitch grows in both directions when wet. Block only to the target measurement and no further; pin at the cast-on edge."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in ends. Wet-block on a head form or bowl. Turn up the brim, pin in place while damp, and allow to dry fully before removing pins."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hand wash cool. Reshape and dry flat. Re-turn the brim while damp if it loses its crisp fold."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The pillbox hat takes the close-fitted crown idea and removes the deep body in favour of a flat, structured top."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}